WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.970
Farewell, Kanuka

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.920
I'd better be off.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.720
Those jerks; they said
they'd come and see you off!

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:41.510
Goodbye.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:44.930
Take care.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.310
You too.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.100
I don't know what to say.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.060
Tell everyone "bye" for me.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.910
There she goes.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.990
You creeps; you're late!

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.700
Actually, we've been here a while.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.160
We were too embarrassed.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.660
Especially after
wrecking her apartment.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.460
You picked a fine time to show it.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.960
Hey, where's Ota?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.320
I take it by your glum faces
she's already left.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:46.870
Captain!

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.790
I wanted to give Kanuka a souvenir,
but I guess I was too late.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.290
Limburger cheese?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.750
That's gonna "raise a stink"
on board the plane.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.670
But it's delicious!
Oh, well, her loss.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.630
Anyone up for lunch
before we leave?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:02.800
Yeah!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.720
And somebody call Ota
to come with us.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.750
Wait! Hold it!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.170
What's this?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.750
New York Police?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.340
You're in Japan.
You can't board the plane armed.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:49.310
Can I have it back as soon
as I leave Japanese airspace?

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.560
Uh...

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:56.440
I'm sure you have your orders,
and I have mine as well.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.520
I need my gun while off-duty.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.490
All I can do is have the captain
hold on to it for you.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:09.200
Then you'd better pray that
I don't need it on board.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.420
Hang on, here.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.220
You didn't think
I was treating, did you?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.050
You mean you aren't?

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.850
How many times do I need to
tell you how small my salary is?

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.390
Want to see my pay stub?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.310
Do you have to be so
depressing during lunch?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.900
Crap, and I ordered
a big steak too.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.780
Noa, can you
lend me some cash?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.990
I don't have much either, so
you have to pay me right back.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.330
Could you drop the money talk
while we're eating?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.540
Save it for after the meal.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.410
Most people think
about it <i>before</i> eating.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:03.380
We wouldn't have to pay, if there
was suddenly a big KABOOM!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.170
Knock it off!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.960
Just kidding.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.010
Sorry, folks, he was just joking.
Nothing to worry about.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.810
Kanuka must have boarded by now.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.290
Afternoon. Don't mind me.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.430
No use,
I just can't wait any longer!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.060
Sir!

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.270
Don't worry.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.730
I'm sorry, but you'll have to
return to your seat.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.070
It's all right. Don't worry.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.240
Sir, it's against regulations!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:15.990
Sir!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.160
Please be seated!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.910
Open up.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.080
The cockpit is off-limits
to passengers!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.630
I know, but I have something
that the captain must see.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:33.220
"This plane has a bomb on it."

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.150
They've stopped.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.940
I wonder if something's wrong.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.290
Maybe it's some kind of prank.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.410
Hang on a minute, would you?

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:07.920
Here we go.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.130
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.420
It's no joke.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.840
I'm hijacking this plane.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.800
Sorry to trouble you.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.680
No trouble at all.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.680
But we haven't taken off yet!

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.020
Well, I hate flying...

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:28.360
so I thought I'd do this
before we took off.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:32.190
But that's not the way
hijacking is done!

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.910
You can't take the passengers
hostage until we're airborne!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.830
I don't like this;
At least wait until we're airborne.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:40.160
Captain!

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:45.580
I'm sorry for breaking tradition,
but the bomb's already in place.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.590
So couldn't you just go along
with my demands?

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.420
I'd appreciate your cooperation.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.590
Freeze!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.800
What did you do that for?

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.640
I was trying to be nice, and
you go and do something like that!

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:06.310
Guns are such a cowardly weapon.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:11.440
You must realize what'd happen
if this went off in here.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.400
It wasn't easy,
smuggling in a ceramic knife.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.080
Honestly, where are they
getting their pilots these days?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.620
I'll hang on to this gun of yours.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.960
Sorry about that.
Are you hurt?

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:34.880
Stop!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:36.840
Who the hell are you?

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.260
This is a restricted area!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:40.800
Yoo-hoo!

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:41.760
Goto!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.890
Long time, no see.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.230
What's going on with that plane?

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.520
Nothing you need to know about.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.900
Except that I have
an officer on board.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:54.690
A police officer?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.150
An extremely competent one.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.740
These are my people.
They're extremely competent too.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.000
Well, that's going a bit far.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.580
- Hi!
- Nice to meet you.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.000
Hello.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.670
Officer Isao Ota, Special Vehicles
Second Section, Division 2.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.010
Yeah, I've heard of you people.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:16.920
Unfounded rumors.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.970
Chief, the captain
is requesting orders.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.220
We have to get that
runway open again!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.140
We'll start negotiations after that.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.230
This wouldn't be a hijack,
would it?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.310
It would.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.940
Whoa! Cool!

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.610
Just like in the movies!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:33.980
How exciting!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.400
I'm glad we came!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.820
Captain, if you need a sniper,
let me volunteer!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.070
For me?

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.370
Thanks so much.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.460
Hello, do you read me?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:49.410
Loud and clear.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.880
This is Doigaki,
head of Air Traffic Control.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.210
Kind of you to call.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.920
This is Ginji Nekowatari,
the hijacker.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.760
What are your demands?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:03.390
I'd like you to release one of the
"Home of the Sea" terrorists.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.600
His name is Itchoku Inubashiri.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.350
I want you to bring him here
to the plane, please and thank you.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.730
Thanks a lot.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:18.490
What do you think?

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.150
He sounds like a rank amateur.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.410
I'm worried about Kanuka.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.580
Yeah, she said
if she missed this flight...

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.490
she couldn't meet her grandmother
in Hawaii during the transfer.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.250
If there's only one hijacker
and he's holed up in the cockpit...

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.500
Kanuka should just smear him!
That'd be a piece of cake for her!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.500
<i>That's</i> what we're worried about.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:38.380
There's the bomb
to think about too.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:45.930
Bomb or not, I'm worried
about that hijacker's safety.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.390
Just what kind of officer is this?

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.930
I told you,
an extremely competent one.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.780
Ma'am!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:02.650
Don't worry.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.580
Ground Defense Force
New Model 97: "Samson"

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.630
There's only one hijacker?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.260
Yes, but he has a bomb!

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.220
- Excuse me, the captain's calling.
- Hang on.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:34.770
It's up to the bigwigs to
decide about Inubashiri's fate.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.020
I wonder if there's some way
to contact our officer on board?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.440
Not likely.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.320
The hijacker's camped out
in the cockpit.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:43.700
Captain!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.410
We could use flag signals!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.070
Kanuka probably
can't read flag signals.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.120
Maybe we could hang a banner out!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.250
What would it say?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.330
"Good luck, Kanuka!"

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.330
- "Good luck"?
- I guess not, huh?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:58.210
What if we sent in
an emergency message?

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.420
We just finished saying
we can't get in touch with her!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.550
Can you find out her seat number?

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.840
The airline would have that info.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.890
- Find out, would you?
- What's her name?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.520
You called?

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.810
Uh...

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:23.240
I feel like I've seen you before.
But where could it have been?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.860
My little sister's on this flight.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.200
Maybe you met her.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.620
Of course, your sister.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.910
And now I'm disturbing
a whole family.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.620
I'm causing trouble for
everyone on board.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:43.170
Could you see that they all
get a nice hot cup of tea?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.090
We'll be sitting here for a while,
so go ahead.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:47.720
Yes, Captain.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.850
No private talk.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.230
Calling 747.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.440
We need a medical check
on the person in seat 8A.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:03.570
8A?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.570
That passenger is flying
to the US for heart surgery...

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.610
and is under the doctor's orders
to avoid unnecessary excitement.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.200
May I talk to them?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:19.620
Passenger 8A had
a minor heart spasm...

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.840
but is now doing well.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.250
Kanuka?

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.590
If this situation is prolonged,
the condition may decline.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.890
Uh, yes indeed.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.720
Dr. Goto,
the airport physician speaking.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.560
The condition is delicate,
so advise the patient to go easy.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.020
I understand, Dr. Goto.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.690
I had no idea there was
a sick person aboard!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.440
How terrible!

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:50.950
I'd better go apologize in person,
and see how he's doing!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.530
No, that might make
things even worse!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:54.450
I'll go.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.620
Well, tell him
that I'm terribly sorry!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.410
Thank you!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.590
How come you think
the bomb is a bluff?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.090
Why set a weapon that
you can't trigger when you need it?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.880
If he had a bomb,
he'd have a detonator switch.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:12.680
And if he had a detonator...

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.930
He'd show us that
instead of a ceramic knife!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.220
One more thing.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.140
He's demanding that Inubashiri
be brought to the plane.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.320
He must be planning to
fly them both to freedom.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:31.820
Would a man who fears flying
set a bomb on his own plane?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.200
Then that means...

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.120
It was all a bluff to
get into the cockpit.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.830
Ginji Nekowatari. Chauffeur.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.210
No crimes or traffic violations.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.500
No connection with
the "Home of the Sea."

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.090
I don't get it.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:52.550
Aha! He's from the
same town as Inubashiri!

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:54.680
So what if he is?

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.510
He'd hardly hijack a plane
to save a childhood friend.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:58.970
That's a laugh.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.680
Maybe he owes him a favor.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:04.650
That's a bit much for a favor.
You're so out of touch.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:08.110
Maybe he's too nice
for his own good.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.070
He's acting alone...

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:14.570
so we may not even
get a chance to help.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:16.570
Shall we go sightseeing?

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.910
Captain, isn't that
a little irresponsible?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:24.170
Well, it's not like an Ingram
could hold back a jumbo jet.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.670
"Miss Extremely Competent"
is back on the line.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:30.130
Message from passenger
8A to Dr. Goto.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:33.510
Fluffy may fall out
a second floor window.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.720
Please alert
Alphonse and his friends.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:37.550
Will do.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.470
Does the passenger in 8A
have a cat?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.180
Apparently.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.890
So who's Alphonse?

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.480
I think he's a dog.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:50.860
He was raised with Fluffy and
never realized Fluffy was a cat.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.740
I'm just the opposite,
unfortunately.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.410
I got along with
my friend Itchoku.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.700
But I never realized
he was such a dirty dog.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.910
Oh, well.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.750
That's the way it goes.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.290
Fluffy's a cat's name, isn't it?

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.750
She means Nekowatari.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.880
And a second-floor window
would be...

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.960
A window on the second floor,
obviously!

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.550
Is your brain still
up there, somewhere?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.010
Speak to your elders with RESPECT!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.720
I'll spell out what
Kanuka's telling us, shall I?

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.350
"Nekowatari will fall out
of a second floor window."

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.480
But windows on planes
don't open, therefore... uh...

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:28.190
Now I get it.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:29.860
Precisely.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:34.780
But we'll never get the Ingram
Alphonse here in time.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.780
Then we'll just have to use
his friends, won't we.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:38.780
Right, Izumi?

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:39.700
Huh?

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.300
Hello! I have good news!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.010
They're releasing Inubashiri?

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.760
No, no news on that yet.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.350
But Dr. Goto said that he's
spoken to the patient's family...

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.970
and wanted to let everyone know
that Fluffy is being taken care of!

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.680
That's wonderful.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.770
I'm going to tell the good news
to the passenger in 8A!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.150
- That'll make him feel better!
- I'll do it!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.440
No, you have work to do.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.610
Besides, I'm bored in the cockpit.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:16.820
Wait!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.140
You!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.430
Passenger 8A is in back,
lying down.

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:49.100
Liar!

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:52.810
You were sitting next to me!
It wasn't your sister!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.030
You totally made that up,
about your sister!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.780
You're disturbing the passengers.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.450
Save it!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.490
You're no stewardess!
Who are you?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.080
Stay back, I'm warning you!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.200
I can't guarantee
I won't hurt someone!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.090
Noa, can you handle that Ingram?

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.460
I can get it moving, but...

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:18.590
But what?

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.050
It takes a lot of muscle.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.090
Just go slow and low.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.350
Don't come any closer,
I'm warning ya!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.150
Put down your knife.
There's nowhere to run.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.760
The end.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.970
I know how to use this thing.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:04.590
You win.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.180
Wait!

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.020
What are you doing?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:12.560
I'm getting off.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:17.020
You can't get off!
This isn't like a train or a taxi!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.110
We're as high as
a two-story building!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.030
It's Inubashiri!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.410
Where?

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.330
Itchoku!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:31.960
Sorry.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.000
Sorry, did that hurt?

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:42.340
No, but that was a dirty,
rotten trick!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:47.800
Even with the safety off,
you still have to chamber a bullet.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.690
Not fair! I wanted go to
Hawaii with Itchoku!

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.650
Chill out, would ya!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.230
Kanuka, this is from Captain Goto.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:06.700
Thank you.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:09.740
Bye.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:11.870
Noa!

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:25.590
Bye.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:47.990
This smells rotten.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:15.770
Izumi!
Postcard from Kanuka.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:17.440
From Kanuka?

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.150
What does she have to say?

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:21.900
Let me see.

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:24.030
"I'll be back."

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:27.990
That's all?

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:37.620
"I'll come back some time."

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.670
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:49.380
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:55.640
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:05.150
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:08.070
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:12.660
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.330
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:20.160
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:24.340
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:30.840
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:36.100
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:38.640
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.850
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.940
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:52.110
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:58.160
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:04.790
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.460
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.460
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:17.600
Shinshi takes Clancy's place,
commanding unit 2.

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:19.560
That was Captain Goto's order.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:22.810
But Shinshi's so lousy,
it's hard to watch. Poor guy.

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:23.770
Things only get worse...

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:27.150
when he gets a job offer
from a software company.

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:29.440
Tamiko, what should I do?

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:31.740
Should I stay, or should I quit?

00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:33.450
Coming next, "Spring Storm."

00:24:33.820 --> 00:24:35.280
Target: Locked on!

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:40.500
Next episode

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:40.500
Spring Storm
